Hi Counterscapes team,

On a phone, counterscapes.com opens with your logo, your number and four larg=
e menu buttons; the first countertop photo only appears after scrolling.

I'm Nathanael from Northframe, a website design studio. I built a private con=
cept for Counterscapes, with your work on the first screen of a phone and a s=
ide-by-side guide to the six materials you offer.

Attached are a short PDF and a 15-second scroll video. It's an independent pr=
oposal; nothing on your site has changed.

We're also piloting an assistant that texts back missed callers, so no job re=
quest gets lost.

Would this direction suit Counterscapes?

Best,
